# Store every text file with LF in the repository AND check it out as LF on
# every platform, so the Windows and the Linux working trees agree byte-for-byte
# and line endings stop churning between the two machines.
#
# NOTE: this repo has `core.autocrlf=true` set locally, which has been checking
# files out as CRLF. `eol=lf` overrides that, so the FIRST checkout/reset after
# this lands rewrites the working tree from CRLF to LF. That is the one-time
# renormalisation — it is why this file is a commit of its own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Learn Anywhere data files are JSON that packages/core's "canonical format
# examples ... re-encode losslessly" test compares BYTE FOR BYTE against the
# serializer output (which always emits \n). Checking one out as CRLF fails that
# test, so pin them explicitly rather than relying on the wildcard above.
*.vok text eol=lf
*.inf text eol=lf
*.sta text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted (a stray CRLF->LF pass would
# corrupt the bundled fonts and the Windows icon).
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
